#### Pitfall 5: Not Propagating User Context in Service-to-Service Calls

**Problem:** Original user identity lost when microservices call each other, breaking audit trails.

**Solution:** Propagate original JWT through service call chain.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD: Service account token loses user context
var serviceToken = GenerateServiceAccountToken();
httpClient.DefaultRequestHeaders.Add("Authorization", $"Bearer {serviceToken}");
// Audit logs show "service-account" not original user

// ✅ GOOD: Propagate original user token
var userToken = _httpContextAccessor.HttpContext.Request.Headers["Authorization"];
httpClient.DefaultRequestHeaders.Add("Authorization", userToken);
// Audit logs show original user through entire call chain
```

