#### Pitfall 6: Algorithm Confusion Attacks (Accepting Multiple Algorithms)

**Problem:** Attacker changes algorithm from RS256 to HS256, uses public key as HMAC secret.

**Solution:** Explicitly require RS256, reject other algorithms.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD: Accepting any algorithm
var token = handler.ReadJwtToken(tokenString);
// Attacker changes alg: RS256 → HS256, signs with public key

// ✅ GOOD: Explicitly validate algorithm
var validatedToken = handler.ValidateToken(tokenString, validationParameters, out var securityToken);
if (securityToken is JwtSecurityToken jwt)
{
    if (jwt.Header.Alg != SecurityAlgorithms.RsaSha256)
    {
        throw new SecurityTokenValidationException("Only RS256 algorithm accepted");
    }
}
```

