### Example 2: Mobile App Offline Access

**Scenario:** Member using Gainwell Go™ mobile app needs to view health records and benefit information while offline (e.g., in subway, airplane).

**Implementation:**

```typescript
// Mobile app authentication and token refresh
class MobileAuthService {
  async login(username: string, password: string) {
    // 1. Authenticate and get tokens
    const response = await fetch('https://auth.gainwell.com/oauth/token', {
      method: 'POST',
      body: new URLSearchParams({
        grant_type: 'password',
        username,
        password,
        client_id: 'gainwell-go-mobile',
        scope: 'patient:read appointments:read benefits:read'
      })
    });

    const tokens = await response.json();

    // 2. Store tokens securely (iOS Keychain / Android Keystore)
    await SecureStore.setItemAsync('access_token', tokens.access_token);
    await SecureStore.setItemAsync('refresh_token', tokens.refresh_token);

    // 3. Decode access token to extract user info
    const payload = jwtDecode(tokens.access_token);
    console.log('Logged in as member:', payload.sub);

    // 4. Schedule background refresh before expiration
    this.scheduleTokenRefresh(tokens.access_token);
  }

  scheduleTokenRefresh(accessToken: string) {
    const payload: any = jwtDecode(accessToken);
    const expiresIn = (payload.exp * 1000) - Date.now();
    const refreshAt = expiresIn - 60000; // Refresh 1 minute before expiration

    if (refreshAt > 0) {
      setTimeout(async () => {
        await this.refreshAccessToken();
      }, refreshAt);
    }
  }

  async refreshAccessToken() {
    const refreshToken = await SecureStore.getItemAsync('refresh_token');

    try {
      const response = await fetch('https://auth.gainwell.com/oauth/token', {
        method: 'POST',
        body: new URLSearchParams({
          grant_type: 'refresh_token',
          refresh_token: refreshToken,
          client_id: 'gainwell-go-mobile'
        })
      });

      const tokens = await response.json();

      // Store new access token
      await SecureStore.setItemAsync('access_token', tokens.access_token);

      // Schedule next refresh
      this.scheduleTokenRefresh(tokens.access_token);

      console.log('Access token refreshed successfully');
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Token refresh failed:', error);
      // User must re-login
      this.logout();
    }
  }

  async makeApiCall(endpoint: string) {
    const accessToken = await SecureStore.getItemAsync('access_token');

    // Check if token expired (offline scenario)
    const payload: any = jwtDecode(accessToken);
    if (payload.exp * 1000 < Date.now()) {
      // Token expired, try refresh if online
      if (await this.isOnline()) {
        await this.refreshAccessToken();
        return this.makeApiCall(endpoint); // Retry with new token
      } else {
        // Offline and token expired, return cached data
        return this.getCachedData(endpoint);
      }
    }

    return fetch(endpoint, {
      headers: {
        'Authorization': `Bearer ${accessToken}`
      }
    });
  }
}
```

**Offline Capability:**
- **Token caching**: Access token valid for 15 minutes, usable offline during that window
- **Data caching**: API responses cached locally, served when offline
- **Background refresh**: Token automatically refreshed when app regains connectivity
- **Refresh token lifetime**: 30 days allows extended offline usage

**Measured Results:**
- **Offline access window**: 15 minutes per access token, 30 days with refresh token
- **Refresh success rate**: 99.3% (automatic retry on network errors)
- **User re-authentication**: Once every 30 days (refresh token expiration)
- **Security**: Tokens stored in encrypted iOS Keychain / Android Keystore (not localStorage)

