[HttpPost]
[Authorize(Policy = "ClaimsWrite")]
public async Task<IActionResult> CreateClaim([FromBody] ClaimRequest request)
{
    // Extract user from JWT (propagated through Connect Engine)
    var userId = User.FindFirst(JwtRegisteredClaimNames.Sub)?.Value;
    var npi = User.FindFirst("npi")?.Value;
    var purposeOfUse = User.FindFirst("purposeOfUse")?.Value;

    // Audit log captures ORIGINAL user context
    _auditLogger.Log(new AuditEntry
    {
        EventType = "CLAIM_CREATED",
        UserId = userId,       // Provider user ID (not "service-account")
        UserNPI = npi,         // Provider NPI
        ResourceType = "Claim",
        ResourceId = newClaim.Id,
        PurposeOfUse = purposeOfUse,  // "Payment"
        SourceSystem = "EDI",
        Timestamp = DateTime.UtcNow
    });

    return Ok(newClaim);
}
```

**Benefits:**
- **Complete audit trail**: Audit logs show original provider, not generic "connect-engine" service account
- **User-level authorization**: Claims API enforces provider-specific rules (NPI validation, state assignments)
- **Compliance**: HIPAA audit requirements met with user attribution through entire call chain
- **Security**: No long-lived service account tokens, each request uses short-lived user token
